        <briefdescription>
<para>This function validates SLH-DSA sign parameters. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ParamsPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to <ref refid="struct_x_asu___slhdsa_sign_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_SlhdsaSignParams</ref>.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS, if validation succeeds.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_INVALID_PARAM, if any field is invalid (NULL pointer, zero addresses, invalid ParamSet, CtxLen/CtxAddr mismatch, MsgLen exceeds DMA limit, SignatureLen mismatch, or SkLen not equal to the ParamSet secret-key size). </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>Validate input pointer.</para><para>Validate the parameter set first, since the expected signature size and the required pre-hash function are both derived from it.</para><para>Validate the context length against the FIPS 205 limit of 255 bytes.</para><para>Validate that a context address is supplied whenever a non-empty context is used.</para><para>Bound the message length by what the ASU DMA can transfer in a single operation, as the message is fed to the hash engine without being split.</para><para>The secret key, message and signature addresses are all mandatory, so a zero address in any of them is rejected before ASUFW dereferences it.</para><para>The secret key is a fixed length per parameter set, so SkLen must match exactly. A caller declaring any other length has not supplied the whole key.</para><para>SLH-DSA signatures are a fixed length per parameter set, so SignatureLen must match exactly. This is what guarantees the output buffer is large enough to be written.</para><para>Validate the pure versus pre-hash message mode, and in pre-hash mode that HashId is the one required by the parameter set and MsgLen is the matching digest length.</para><para>Validate the sign mode, which selects hedged or deterministic signing. </para>        </inbodydescription>
